ALGORITM

Start the program
Define a base class Animal
Declare a private variable name (Encapsulation)
Create a method speak() with no implementation (Abstraction)
Create a method to access the private variable
Define a derived class Dog that inherits from Animal (Inheritance)
Override the speak() method in Dog
Define another derived class Cat that inherits from Animal
Override the speak() method in Cat (Polymorphism)
Create objects of Dog and Cat
Call the speak() method for both objects
Display the results
Stop the program

code 

class Animal:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.__name = name    
    def speak(self):
        pass   
    def get_name(self):
        return self.__name
class Dog(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        return self.get_name() + " says Woof"
class Cat(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        return self.get_name() + " says Meow"
d = Dog("Buddy")
c = Cat("Kitty")
print(d.speak())
print(c.speak())


